<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We study entropic versions of four-function inequalities and give transport proofs of the Euclidean Ahlswede–Daykin theorem and
a four-function version of the Prékopa–Leindler inequality due to Cordero-Erausquin and Maurey.
One of our main results shows that the sharp range for the four-function inequality for equally weighted power means of finite orders <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math>
is <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\alpha+\beta\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\alpha+\beta\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, with the Ahlswede–Daykin min–max inequality obtained as a limit.
En route, we prove corresponding entropy inequalities under the quadratic optimal transport coupling,
including an entropy power inequality for the minimum and maximum in Euclidean space.
We also study the stability of four-function inequalities under convolution with log-concave product densities,
recovering the preservation of log-supermodularity established by Karlin and Rinott, and
explain its application to a conditional entropy power inequality for log-supermodular random variables.</p>
  
