<div id="S6.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that
<math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}^{j}\longrightarrow\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}^{j}\longrightarrow\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}^{j}\longrightarrow\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}^{j}\longrightarrow\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
in <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal coupling between <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the optimal coupling <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is unique, then
<math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{j}\longrightarrow\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{j}\longrightarrow\pi</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently,</span></p>
