<div id="S6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the stability of optimal transport plans
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, Theorem 5.20]</cite>, every weak limit point of
<math id="S6.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal coupling of <math id="S6.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the
assumed uniqueness of that coupling,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{j}\rightharpoonup\pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇀</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{j}\rightharpoonup\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\bigl(|x|^{2}+|y|^{2}\bigr)\,d\pi_{j}(x,y)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|x|^{2}\,d\nu_{1}^{j}(x)+\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|y|^{2}\,d\nu_{2}^{j}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\bigl(|x|^{2}+|y|^{2}\bigr)\,d\pi_{j}(x,y)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|x|^{2}\,d\nu_{1}^{j}(x)+\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|y|^{2}\,d\nu_{2}^{j}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the right-hand side converges to the corresponding expression for
<math id="S6.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. The characterization of Wasserstein convergence
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, Theorem 6.9]</cite> therefore yields</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

