<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{j}\longrightarrow\pi\qquad\text{in }W_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{j}\longrightarrow\pi\qquad\text{in }W_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{2d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">The coordinatewise maps</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{-}(x,y)=x\wedge y,\qquad m_{+}(x,y)=x\vee y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{-}(x,y)=x\wedge y,\qquad m_{+}(x,y)=x\vee y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">are <math id="S6.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz from <math id="S6.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
pushforward by an <math id="S6.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz map is <math id="S6.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in Wasserstein
distance
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Lemma 4.1]</cite>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\bigl((m_{\pm})_{\#}\pi_{j},(m_{\pm})_{\#}\pi\bigr)\leq W_{2}(\pi_{j},\pi)\longrightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\bigl((m_{\pm})_{\#}\pi_{j},(m_{\pm})_{\#}\pi\bigr)\leq W_{2}(\pi_{j},\pi)\longrightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p13" class="ltx_para">
