</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p14.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to prove Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3 The Euclidean Ahlswede–Daykin 4-function theorem ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> in the regular case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bounded, smooth, uniformly convex domain. Suppose that <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have densities smooth on <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{K}</annotation></semantics></math> that are bounded above and below by positive constants. Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)\leq H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)\leq H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use Caffarelli’s global regularity theory for the second boundary
value problem for the Monge–Ampère equation
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. The hypotheses of the result used here are that
the source and target supports are bounded uniformly convex domains
with <math id="S6.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> boundaries and, for some <math id="S6.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, that their
densities extend to functions in <math id="S6.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> on the closures of the
respective domains and satisfy two-sided bounds</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c\leq n_{i}\leq C&lt;\infty,\qquad i\in\{1,2\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c\leq n_{i}\leq C&lt;\infty,\qquad i\in\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">These hypotheses hold here, with both source and target domains equal
to <math id="S6.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="S6.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> has smooth boundary and the densities are smooth on <math id="S6.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and
bounded above and below by positive constants. The cited regularity
theory therefore gives <math id="S6.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in C^{2,\alpha}(\overline{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in C^{2,\alpha}(\overline{K})</annotation></semantics></math>. The
Monge–Ampère equation and the two-sided density bounds imply that
<math id="S6.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det D^{2}\varphi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det D^{2}\varphi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; since <math id="S6.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, <math id="S6.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore
positive definite. In particular,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\nabla\varphi\colon K\longrightarrow K" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\nabla\varphi\colon K\longrightarrow K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">is a diffeomorphism and</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)\coloneqq DT(x)=D^{2}\varphi(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)\coloneqq DT(x)=D^{2}\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">is symmetric and positive definite. Since <math id="S6.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, integration
of <math id="S6.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> along line segments shows that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle T(x)-T(y),x-y\rangle&gt;0\qquad(x\neq y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle T(x)-T(y),x-y\rangle&gt;0\qquad(x\neq y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p15.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p15.5.1" class="ltx_text">so Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 6.1. ‣ 6 A transport proof of the min–max entropy inequality ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> applies.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, the maps</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{-}(x)=x\wedge T(x),\qquad T_{+}(x)=x\vee T(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{-}(x)=x\wedge T(x),\qquad T_{+}(x)=x\vee T(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">are injective.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a point <math id="S6.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> at which <math id="S6.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> are differentiable, and set</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=I(x)=\{i:x_{i}\leq T_{i}(x)\},\qquad J=I^{c}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=I(x)=\{i:x_{i}\leq T_{i}(x)\},\qquad J=I^{c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">At almost every such point, the Jacobian of <math id="S6.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by taking
the <math id="S6.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row from the identity matrix for <math id="S6.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S6.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th
row from <math id="S6.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in J</annotation></semantics></math>. On the set where <math id="S6.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=T_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=T_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the two
rows agree almost everywhere, since the gradient of the <math id="S6.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> function
<math id="S6.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}-T_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}-T_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes almost everywhere on its zero set. Thus the
choice made in the definition of <math id="S6.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> causes no ambiguity. After
reordering the coordinates so that
the indices in <math id="S6.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> come first,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT_{-}(x)=\begin{pmatrix}\operatorname{Id}_{I}&amp;0\\
A_{JI}(x)&amp;A_{JJ}(x)\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT_{-}(x)=\begin{pmatrix}\operatorname{Id}_{I}&amp;0\\
A_{JI}(x)&amp;A_{JJ}(x)\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT_{+}(x)=\begin{pmatrix}A_{II}(x)&amp;A_{IJ}(x)\\
0&amp;\operatorname{Id}_{J}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT_{+}(x)=\begin{pmatrix}A_{II}(x)&amp;A_{IJ}(x)\\
0&amp;\operatorname{Id}_{J}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S6.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det DT_{-}(x)=\det A_{JJ}(x),\qquad\det DT_{+}(x)=\det A_{II}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det DT_{-}(x)=\det A_{JJ}(x),\qquad\det DT_{+}(x)=\det A_{II}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the determinant of an empty principal minor is understood to be
equal to <math id="S6.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S6.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite, Fischer’s determinant inequality
gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det A(x)\leq\det A_{II}(x)\det A_{JJ}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det A(x)\leq\det A_{II}(x)\det A_{JJ}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">Together with (<a href="#S6.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 6 A transport proof of the min–max entropy inequality ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), this yields</span></p>
<table id="S6.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det DT(x)\leq\det DT_{-}(x)\det DT_{+}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det DT(x)\leq\det DT_{-}(x)\det DT_{+}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">for almost every <math id="S6.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S6.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1},n_{2},n_{-},n_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1},n_{2},n_{-},n_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the densities of
<math id="S6.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1},\nu_{2},\nu_{-},\nu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1},\nu_{2},\nu_{-},\nu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Since <math id="S6.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> are
injective, the area formula gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{-}(T_{-}(x))\det DT_{-}(x)=n_{1}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{-}(T_{-}(x))\det DT_{-}(x)=n_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{+}(T_{+}(x))\det DT_{+}(x)=n_{1}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{+}(T_{+}(x))\det DT_{+}(x)=n_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">for almost every <math id="S6.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)-\int_{K}\log\det DT_{-}(x)\,d\nu_{1}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)-\int_{K}\log\det DT_{-}(x)\,d\nu_{1}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)-\int_{K}\log\det DT_{+}(x)\,d\nu_{1}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)-\int_{K}\log\det DT_{+}(x)\,d\nu_{1}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p19.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p19.4.1" class="ltx_text">Adding these identities gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\nu_{-}\mid\lambda)+H(\nu_{+}\mid\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
