<p id="S7.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Both diagonal matrices are positive. Apply
Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 7.4. ‣ 7.2 A scalar criterion and its transport proof ‣ 7 Connections with Prékopa–Leindler in the continuous setting ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a> to both Jacobians, using the
same pivots <math id="S7.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. By
(<a href="#S7.E23" title="In Theorem 7.6 (A scalar criterion for power-mean inequalities). ‣ 7.2 A scalar criterion and its transport proof ‣ 7 Connections with Prékopa–Leindler in the continuous setting ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S7.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

