<div id="S7.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.7</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Entropy inequality for coordinatewise power means)<span id="S7.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1},\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1},\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> be as in
Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 7.6 (A scalar criterion for power-mean inequalities). ‣ 7.2 A scalar criterion and its transport proof ‣ 7 Connections with Prékopa–Leindler in the continuous setting ‣ Four Function Theorems Through Optimal Transport and Entropic Analogs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>. For <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,\theta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,\theta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, put
<math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{q}^{\theta}=(M_{q}^{\theta})_{\#}\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{q}^{\theta}=(M_{q}^{\theta})_{\#}\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S7.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\nu_{q}^{\theta}\mid\lambda)\leq\theta H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+(1-\theta)H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\nu_{q}^{\theta}\mid\lambda)\leq\theta H(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+(1-\theta)H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,r,s,t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,r,s,t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=rs+(1-r)t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=rs+(1-r)t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S7.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rH((M_{\alpha}^{s})_{\#}\pi\mid\lambda)+(1-r)H((M_{\beta}^{t})_{\#}\pi\mid\lambda)\leq mH(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+(1-m)H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rH((M_{\alpha}^{s})_{\#}\pi\mid\lambda)+(1-r)H((M_{\beta}^{t})_{\#}\pi\mid\lambda)\leq mH(\nu_{1}\mid\lambda)+(1-m)H(\nu_{2}\mid\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
